  "2026-10-13T18:12:38.703Z","harness:codex","{\"text\":\"Duplicate check: complete live2953-item all-status corpus plus search/open/in-progress reads. Full closed pm-9djr6d implements linked-test editing with provenance; full closed pm-pae3wo implements real two-prior-release matrix for unknown top-level extension fields. Current matrix source tests top-level fields but does not exercise tests_update nested stamps. No existing open owner for this specific reported regression was found. Issue1458 and all paginated comments including independent pm-github occurrence6149865337 read. Treat external reproduction as reported evidence until independently reproduced; retain shipped predecessors and relate them rather than reopening unrelated completed scopes.\"}"
  "2026-10-13T18:39:55.336Z","harness:codex","Hosted static CI38446450129 correctly caught the missing expected_result in this newly created intake. Added the explicit intended outcome through PM without changing acceptance criteria, implementation scope or gate thresholds. This planning correction does not claim the reported feature/defect is implemented."
  "2026-10-14T04:11:45.727Z","harness:codex","Live intake: full issue body, both external occurrences, canonical linked-test editor and published-workspace matrix metadata/history read. Older published hosts cannot be retroactively patched; reproduce exact legacy artifacts first and use a declared storage compatibility boundary where new persisted nested fields cannot be represented safely. Preserve immutable history and avoid re-anchoring."
  "2026-10-14T04:35:05.914Z","harness:codex","Independent real-artifact reproduction confirms 2026.10.9 and10.10 silently omit tests_update editor stamps and fail after_hash/current_item_hash commitments while10.13 verifies identical bytes. Additional marker probe proves10.9 predates future-format admission, whereas10.10/13 safely refuse format2. Therefore protect current writes when authoritative project pins select pre-10.10 hosts, retain readable format1, write format2 only when needed, preserve prior history prefixes and minimum format through restoration/merge. Existing legacy format1 editor commitments stay unchanged during read; ordinary real writes append the explicit upgrade. Supported format2 operation requires coordinated verifier/SDK/CI/merge-driver upgrade;9 is only a historical baseline writer, never an admitted guarded reader."
  "2026-10-14T05:41:05.035Z","harness:codex","Full-suite regression investigation corrected baseline creation receipts: do not add an own undefined pm_format_version property, because consumers can serialize it as invalid legacy data. All33 focused get/reopen/evidence-consistency/cursor keepers now pass. The seven-row real-artifact matrix retains its full acceptance and has an eight-minute bound for contention during whole-suite coverage; no cases or quality thresholds were removed. Declared semver ranges, upper-only ranges, disjunctions and wildcard pins are checked using the existing locked semver7.8.5 payload, with eligible7.8.0 types. Opaque references retain resolved-host admission. Final full coverage and hosted delivery remain pending."
  "2026-10-14T06:09:18.240Z","harness:codex","Full coverage passes10420 tests with3 retained platform skips; the strict integer gate detects two uncovered branches. Creation only admits fresh linked-test values without editor stamps, so removed its unreachable format-upgrade branch instead of forging a test or ignoring coverage. Real nested editor mutations remain guarded in the shared store, restore and merge. Source-level wrong-cursor recovery is added to the existing pagination keeper. Linked test timeout during concurrent full-suite lease contention is retained and will be rerun after that owner exits; no test case or threshold was removed."
  "2026-10-14T06:13:26.405Z","harness:codex","Final linked verification passes via pm test --run --progress, including all4 baseline directions plus3 reported-version nested-field rows using actual npm artifacts, native Git merge drivers, exact nested values, immutable history prefixes and unchanged-byte old-host refusal. Packed npm/npx/bunx and Node/Bun SDK evaluation,9-package dogfood, unchanged40-package runtime ledger and migration acceptance pass. Current source adds no creation-time marker; fresh tests stay baseline1 and actual editor/store writes carry2. Whole-suite10420 tests passed; exact100% rerun and final reviewed delivery remain required."
  "2026-10-14T06:48:53.489Z","harness:codex","Final complete source acceptance passes10420 tests with3 retained platform skips at exact100/100/100/100. Linked105 cases include actual four-direction baseline and three historical nested-field rows, public SDK/hash/value preservation, restore and native Git reconciliation. Legacy format1 stays current; future-format admission refuses before loss. Current health/validate have0 unreadable, parse, future-format, drift or pending merge problems;7 legacy terminal hierarchy warnings are retained. CLI-generated closure and upstream pm-changelog2026.10.13 generation will be reviewed with the source; no post-merge direct-main evidence commit is planned."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-14T06:03:21.328Z","harness:codex","Preserving nested fields in a new runtime cannot repair older published canonicalizers. Put the reader requirement on the same real write as the new nested fields, retain that requirement while newer history survives restore or merge, and independently prove which oldest hosts actually enforce it."
